# Git: new branch per work session

When starting a new task or continuing after a completed PR/commit wave:

- **Create a new branch first** — do not keep committing on the previous feature branch.
- Name branches by intent, e.g. `fix/…`, `feat/…`, `chore/…`.
- **Base on the newest shipped tip** — the latest production-deployed feature branch (or `main`/`dev` only if it already contains that tip). Never cut from a stale `dev` that lags Prizelet branding or recent polish.
- Before branching: `git fetch` and confirm the base has current package/branding (e.g. `prizelet`, `PrizeletLogo`) and recent layout work.
- Commit only when asked (or when the user explicitly requests push/PR); then **push the new branch** and **open a new PR**.
- Prefer a focused PR for the current change set; do not dump unrelated work onto an old branch.

## Examples

```bash
# ✅ Start from newest tip (example: last shipped polish branch)
git fetch origin
git checkout fix/global-segmented-controls   # or whatever is currently live
git pull
git checkout -b fix/admin-wave2-people-tables

# ❌ Cut from outdated upstream and overwrite prod
git checkout origin/dev   # stale — missing Prizelet / polish
git checkout -b fix/something
npx vercel --prod         # can roll branding back
```

Stack onto an existing feature branch only when the user asks for a stacked PR or the change depends on unmerged work on that branch.
